{"success": true, "message": "Test details sent successfully", "data": {"test": {"_id": "69de21f37e39d99b57bc5b36", "analysisVideoCdn": "yt", "exam": ["605dfcb2f226ac25a8bd5fef"], "ctype": null, "position": 0, "order": 12, "enableCalculator": false, "isContinuousQuestion": false, "reattemptAvailable": false, "singleSectionMultipleSubjects": false, "timeRestricted": false, "title": "Chemical Bonding and Molecular Structure - Test 4", "description": "Previous Year Questions as Chapter Test", "syllabus": "This test contains questions from all topics of this chapter included in the JEE Main syllabus. It includes a mix of questions from PYQs of JEE Main 2019 - 2025.", "totalTime": 37, "totalQuestions": 25, "totalMarks": 100, "bonusQuestions": null, "bonusMarks": null, "startDate": "2026-04-15T03:30:00.000Z", "endDate": "2027-04-30T00:00:00.000Z", "type": "free", "class": "605df635a37b7025c438d685", "instruction": "608289ffb160b022e9442c83", "subjects": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "totalMarks": 100, "bonusMarks": 0, "totalQuestions": 25, "bonusQuestions": 0, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924c00d"}], "sections": [{"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfc6", "title": "Chemistry Single Correct", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf5f", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6117b88f67dbe2603c3e80be"], "question": {"text": "<p>Statement I : Sodium hydride can be used as an oxidising agent.</p><p>Statement II : The lone pair of electrons on nitrogen in pyridine makes it basic.</p><p>Choose the CORRECT answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "a3563c", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf60"}, {"id": "8aa84b", "text": "Statement I is true but statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf61"}, {"id": "f56f7f", "text": "Statement I is false but statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf62"}, {"id": "ccb398", "text": "Both statement I and statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf63"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf64", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b64"], "question": {"text": "<p>Bonding in which of the following diatomic molecule(s) become(s) stronger, on the basis of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MO</mi></math> Theory, by removal of an electron?</p><p>(A) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi></math></p><p>(B) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(C) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(D) <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>(E)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math></p><p>Choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1745fa", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf65"}, {"id": "99db37", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf66"}, {"id": "da58d5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf67"}, {"id": "dc4704", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf68"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf69", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4771"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87e0"], "question": {"text": "Which one of the following pairs is an example of polar molecular solids?"}, "options": [{"id": "548cab", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf6a"}, {"id": "1362eb", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf6b"}, {"id": "e07e8f", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MgO</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf6c"}, {"id": "e9b618", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HCl</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mi>AlN</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf6d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf6e", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["61ab79db6fe44bfe0fe4b3bb"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> and the other is labelled as Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced><mo>.</mo></math><br/>Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced><mo>:</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> has lower boiling point than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>.</mo></math><br/>Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced><mo>:</mo></math> In liquid state <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> molecules are associated through Vander Waal's forces, but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>PH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> molecules are associated through hydrogen bonding.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "0efc12", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math> are correct and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math> is not the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf6f"}, {"id": "132653", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> is not correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math> is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf70"}, {"id": "6e6fab", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math> are correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math> is the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf71"}, {"id": "e4153a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mfenced></math> is correct but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mfenced></math> is not correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf72"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf73", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b3f"], "question": {"text": "The shape/structure of<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>5</mn></msub></mfenced><mo>-</mo></msup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, respectively are :"}, "options": [{"id": "0be207", "text": "pentagonal planar and trigonal bipyramidal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf74"}, {"id": "b9b193", "text": "octahedral and square pyramidal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf75"}, {"id": "977f2f", "text": "trigonal bipyramidal and pentagonal planar", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf76"}, {"id": "694a7e", "text": "trigonal bipyramidal and trigonal bipyramidal", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf77"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf78", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["6162fb826ed13040ec84fbd4"], "question": {"text": "Which of the following linear combination of atomic orbitals will lead to formation of molecular orbitals in homonuclear diatomic molecules [internuclear axis in $z$-direction] ?\nA. $2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{z}}$ and $2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{x}}$\nB. 2 s and $2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{x}}$\nC. $3 \\mathrm{~d}_{\\mathrm{xy}}$ and $3 \\mathrm{~d}_{\\mathrm{x}^2-y^2}$\nD. 2 s and $2 \\mathrm{p}_{\\mathrm{z}}$\nE. $2 p_z$ and $3 d_x{ }^2-y^2$\nChoose the correct answer from the options given below:"}, "options": [{"id": "d1b60e", "text": "A and B Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf79"}, {"id": "811c7c", "text": "D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf7a"}, {"id": "45fea6", "text": "E Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf7b"}, {"id": "dc6492", "text": "C and D Only", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf7c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf7d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95d3"], "question": {"text": "The interaction energy of London forces between two particles is proportional to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi>x</mi></msup></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is the distance between the particles. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is :"}, "options": [{"id": "fcc1bc", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf7e"}, {"id": "d75659", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf7f"}, {"id": "3784df", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf80"}, {"id": "b56ca5", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf81"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf82", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52be"], "question": {"text": "Among the following species, the diamagnetic molecule is:"}, "options": [{"id": "d343c4", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf83"}, {"id": "e0d5e6", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf84"}, {"id": "a0a772", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf85"}, {"id": "c71931", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf86"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf87", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e40fd4f1ef260f84ed1e58"], "question": {"text": "Number of molecules/ions from the following in which the central atom is involved in \\(\\mathrm{sp}^3\\) hybridization is \\(\\qquad\\)\n\\(\\mathrm{NO}_3^{-}, \\mathrm{BCl}_3, \\mathrm{ClO}_2^{-}, \\mathrm{ClO}_3\\)"}, "options": [{"id": "c798a7", "text": "4", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf88"}, {"id": "669530", "text": "3", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf89"}, {"id": "17edc4", "text": "2", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf8a"}, {"id": "be41c3", "text": "1", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf8b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf8c", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["61ada090dedd066c316e5bea"], "question": {"text": "The relative strength of the interionic/ intermolecular forces in a decreasing order is:"}, "options": [{"id": "56dee1", "text": "dipole-dipole&nbsp;<math><mo>&#62;</mo></math>&nbsp;ion-dipole&nbsp;<math><mo>&#62;</mo></math> ion-ion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf8d"}, {"id": "5d040f", "text": "ion-dipole <math><mo>&#62;</mo></math> ion-ion <math><mo>&#62;</mo></math> dipole-dipole", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf8e"}, {"id": "744755", "text": "ion-dipole <math><mo>&gt;</mo></math> dipole-dipole <math><mo>&gt;</mo></math> ion-ion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf8f"}, {"id": "8daa9a", "text": "ion-ion <math><mo>&gt;</mo></math> ion-dipole <math><mo>&gt;</mo></math> dipole-dipole", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf90"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf91", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["6117b89067dbe2603c3e80ce"], "question": {"text": "Which among the following molecules is (a) involved in $\\mathrm{sp}^3 \\mathrm{~d}$ hybridization, (b) has different bond lengths and (c) has lone pair of electrons on the central atom?"}, "options": [{"id": "9a6ff5", "text": "$\\mathrm{PF}_5$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf92"}, {"id": "4cd58c", "text": "$\\mathrm{XeF}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf93"}, {"id": "ab7881", "text": "$\\mathrm{SF}_4$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf94"}, {"id": "4c89dc", "text": "$\\mathrm{XeF}_2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf95"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf96", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["617aa9e9ef3fe65ad8e837eb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Match List-I with List-II</p><table border=\"1\" cellpadding=\"1\" cellspacing=\"1\" style=\"width: 500px;\">\t<tbody>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-I</strong></td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\">&nbsp;</td>\t\t\t<td style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>List-II</strong></td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>A</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mi>MO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>I</td>\t\t\t<td>Dipole moment</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>B</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Q</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math></td>\t\t\t<td>II</td>\t\t\t<td>Bonding molecular orbital</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>C</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></td>\t\t\t<td>III</td>\t\t\t<td>Anti-bonding molecualr orbital</td>\t\t</tr>\t\t<tr>\t\t\t<td>D</td>\t\t\t<td><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mi>MO</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#936;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math></td>\t\t\t<td>IV</td>\t\t\t<td>Bond order</td>\t\t</tr>\t</tbody></table>"}, "options": [{"id": "a3ffd0", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf97"}, {"id": "26bfff", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf98"}, {"id": "bcc42a", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf99"}, {"id": "f677e9", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>III</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>IV</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>II</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf9a"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf9b", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b566b"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements: one is labelled as Assertion <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and the other is labelled as Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>.</p><p>Assertion&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> : Dipole-dipole interactions are the only non-covalent interactions, resulting in hydrogen bond formation.</p><p>Reason <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;: Fluorine is the most electronegative element and hydrogen bonds in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HF</mi></math> are symmetrical.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "829d40", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;is false but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf9c"}, {"id": "f135cf", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;are true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is NOT the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf9d"}, {"id": "ef1a06", "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;is true but <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf9e"}, {"id": "8be79c", "text": "Both <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;are true and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>&nbsp;is the correct explanation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bf9f"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa0", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["6162fb826ed13040ec84fbca"], "question": {"text": "During the change of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></math> to <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> , the incoming electron goes to the orbital:"}, "options": [{"id": "2e9e10", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa1"}, {"id": "6f8c7f", "text": "<math><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></mrow></msup><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa2"}, {"id": "8b38ea", "text": "<math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">π</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa3"}, {"id": "b264b5", "text": "<math><msub><mrow><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">σ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">*</mi></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi></mrow></msub></math>", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa5", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e56813499d1e49588fa394"], "question": {"text": "Given below are two statements :\nStatement (I): Experimentally determined oxygen-oxygen bond lengths in the $\\mathrm{O}_3$ are found to be same and the bond length is greater than that of a $\\mathrm{O}=\\mathrm{O}$ (double bond) but less than that of a single $(O-O)$ bond.\nStatement (II) : The strong lone pair-lone pair repulsion between oxygen atoms is solely responsible for the fact that the bond length in ozone is smaller than that of a double bond $(\\mathrm{O}=\\mathrm{O})$ but more than that of a single bond $(\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{O})$.\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :"}, "options": [{"id": "4fafa3", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa6"}, {"id": "741d84", "text": "Statement I is false but Statement II is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa7"}, {"id": "138f64", "text": "Statement I is true but Statement II is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa8"}, {"id": "25ad1b", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfa9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfaa", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["61ab79db6fe44bfe0fe4b3bb"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements : One is labelled as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Assertion</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and the other is labelled as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Reason</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math>.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Assertion</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math> Butan&ndash;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&ndash;ol has higher boiling point than ethoxyethane.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Reason</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo></math> Extensive hydrogen bonding leads to stronger association of molecules.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "af52db", "text": "A is true but R is false", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfab"}, {"id": "04e05e", "text": "Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfac"}, {"id": "fc6619", "text": "Both A and R are true but R is not the correct explanation of A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfad"}, {"id": "260866", "text": "A is false but R is true", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfae"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfaf", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["6162fb826ed13040ec84fbc7"], "question": {"text": "When \\(\\psi_{\\mathrm{A}}\\) and \\(\\psi_{\\mathrm{B}}\\) are the wave functions of atomic orbitals, then \\(\\sigma^*\\) is represented by :"}, "options": [{"id": "eb205e", "text": "\\(\\psi_{\\mathrm{A}}+2 \\psi_{\\mathrm{B}}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb0"}, {"id": "3cc19e", "text": "\\(\\psi_A-\\psi_B\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb1"}, {"id": "f76181", "text": "\\(\\psi_{\\mathrm{A}}+\\psi_{\\mathrm{B}}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb2"}, {"id": "96b703", "text": "\\(\\psi_A-2 \\psi_B\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb4", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b76"], "concepts": ["60e2fb1f66f9ce3f243b4b3f"], "question": {"text": "<p>Given below are two statements :</p><p>Statement I : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> both possess V-shaped structure</p><p>Statement II : The bond angle of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is less than that of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "4559d4", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb5"}, {"id": "b9b172", "text": "Both Statement I and Statement II are correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb6"}, {"id": "596959", "text": "Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb7"}, {"id": "3848f6", "text": "Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb8"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfb9", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fbdd66f9ce3f243b567c"], "concepts": ["60e567ab499d1e49588f95d3"], "question": {"text": "The predominant intermolecular forces present in ethyl acetate, a liquid, are:"}, "options": [{"id": "eb4a88", "text": "London dispersion and dipole-dipole", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfba"}, {"id": "6df13e", "text": "hydrogen bonding and London dispersion", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfbb"}, {"id": "9f5b46", "text": "Dipole-dipole and hydrogen bonding", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfbc"}, {"id": "6aead3", "text": "London dispersion, dipole-dipole and hydrogen bonding", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfbd"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f2f2ee0e063d924bfbe", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60d2d1d2185d7a32fa3205ae"], "topics": ["60e2fb9e66f9ce3f243b52e8"], "concepts": ["60e567c3499d1e49588f9947"], "question": {"text": "Arrange the following bonds according to their average bond energies in descending order:<br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"